K-quant and IQ integer-dot and DPAS matmul

Folded from the old patches: 0001, 0002, 0004, 0005, 0006, 0009, 0011, 0012, 0013, 0014.

The Intel OpenCL matmul family for K-quant and IQ weights: the integer-dot GEMV, the XMX (DPAS) GEMM with 2D block loads and its tile search, the few-column and few-row variants, and the small decode ops around them.

The old patch files (named in FOLDED.md) are history; the section for each old number
in contrib/llama.cpp/README.md still describes its measurements. This file is the
diff between the tree after the previous folded patch and the tree after this one;
the sum of all folded patches is byte-identical to the old series applied in order.

